{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In the second year, etc.</b> One needs to know why Scripture changed the usual order, which is to mention the month first and then the year — for so you find at the beginning of the book, where it says ״בְּאֶחָד לַחֹדֶשׁ הַשֵּׁנִי בַּשָּׁנָה הַשֵּׁנִית״. Moreover, in this order that it wrote, Scripture was compelled to interrupt in the middle of the mention of the time with the statement <b>when they came out of the land of Egypt</b>, which it would not have done if it had mentioned the month first and then the year, for then it would say ״when they came out of the land of Egypt״ afterward. There is further reason to note why this portion differs in that it does not say ״Speak to the children of Israel״ as in the entire Torah. This, however, will be explained when we further note its saying <b>and they performed</b> with the addition of the vav at the beginning of the matter. It is further difficult why HaShem needed to command the children of Israel regarding the Pesach, seeing that He had already commanded as stated in the portion Bo el Pharaoh (Exodus 12:43). And it might seem one could say regarding this that Scripture was careful to say that the commandment of Pesach applies only in the land of Egypt and when they come to an inhabited land, but not in the wilderness — therefore it comes to say in the wilderness <b>and the children of Israel shall perform the Pesach</b>; but this is far-fetched." "<b>And it appears</b> that the intent of Scripture is as follows. Since the Torah said (Exodus 12:43) ״כָּל בֶּן נֵכָר לֹא יֹאכַל בּוֹ״, and it is taught in the Mekhilta in these words: ״כָּל בֶּן נֵכָר״ — this includes both an apostate Israelite and a gentile, end of their language. And since we find that Israel made the calf, etc., and the Sages of blessed memory said (Ḥulin 5a) that anyone who acknowledges idolatry is as one who denies the entire Torah, and he may be called a בן נכר — from this point there is grounds to judge concerning Israel that they are not able to perform the Pesach. And although HaShem was appeased by Moses through his prayers and through the judgment he executed upon Israel, with all this they had not yet been informed that the sin of the calf had been atoned for, and there is doubt in the matter. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, came and granted permission and said to them <b>and the children of Israel shall perform the Pesach</b>. And Scripture was precise in saying <b>and they shall perform</b> — to say that beyond what they had been assured, that HaShem had relented from the evil He had spoken of doing, they were further rendered fit to be worthy of performing the Pesach." "And from this we now come to understand the reason for the change in placing the mention of the year first. For since the entire purpose of the statement here was only to render them fit to perform the Pesach, therefore at the opening of His words He mentioned <b>the second year</b>, to make known the context of the statement — namely, that this was after the matter of the calf, something that would not be grasped by mentioning the time of the month, which does not convey this implication at all. And therefore it did not say ״Speak to the children of Israel,״ for He did not come to command this but to grant permission, and it was sufficient to make the matter known to Moses, that such is the law. Or perhaps, according to what they said in Pesaḥim (6a) that this statement was on Rosh Ḥodesh, we may say that this statement was before the descent of the Shekhinah to the Mishkan on the first day of the month of Nisan, and HaShem preceded this statement to inform them that they are fit to perform the Pesach, and afterward the Shekhinah descended. And therefore you find that it says immediately after this <b>and on the day that the Mishkan was set up, the cloud covered</b>."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:05.219081838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}